  "pageshortdescription": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "shortDescTitle": "<p><b>Revisions. Simplified.</b></p>\r\n",
    "shortDescTop": "<p>The Triathlon Revision system is designed to provide simplicity in achieving joint stability and fixation. The Triathlon Revision system provides patented implants and instrumentation designed to properly locate the joint line and balance the knee consistently<sup>1</sup>, as well as reaming instrumentation to allow for accurate preparation of metaphyseal fixation.<sup>2-5</sup></p>\r\n",
    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "stephen.brown@stryker.com",
    "hideComponent": "true",
    "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Aug 03 2021 14:55:03 GMT+0000",
    "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/pageshortdescription",
    "textIsRich": [
      "true",
      "true",
      "true"
    ]
  },
  "rte": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "joelle.battista@stryker.com",
    "hideComponent": "true",
    "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
    "text": "<h3>Revisions. Simplified.</h3>\n<p>The Triathlon Revision system is designed to provide simplicity in achieving joint stability and fixation. The Triathlon Revision system provides patented implants and instrumentation designed to properly locate the joint line and balance the knee consistently1, as well as reaming instrumentation to allow for accurate preparation of metaphyseal fixation.<sup>2-5</sup></p>\n<h5>Joint line</h5>\n<p>Triathlon TS is designed to facilitate joint line restoration, which aids in reducing issues such as decreased motion, decreased extensor strength, anterior knee pain, and midflexion instability.</p>\n<h5>Stability</h5>\n<p>The anatomic location of the Triathlon TS femoral boss reduces the need for offsetting to provide flexion stability<sup>6</sup>; additionally, Triathlon TS’s insert geometry allows for varus/valgus stability with rotational freedom.<sup>6,7</sup></p>\n<h5>Fixation</h5>\n<p>Cone preparation and implants provide an intimate, line-to-line fit, which allows for accurate Triathlon Tritanium Cone Augment positioning and initial fixation.<sup>5,7,8,9,10</sup></p>\n<h5>Balance</h5>\n<p>The single radius is designed to restore the knee’s single center of rotation during active flexion, allowing for constant ligament balance and enhanced stability in flexion.<sup>11-16</sup></p>\n",
    "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Nov 25 2025 17:33:33 GMT+0000",
    "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
    "textIsRich": "true"
  },
